00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.210
Episode 6: Different Paths

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.210
Episode 6: Different Paths

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.210
What are you two doing this early in the morning?!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.500
Just what were you thinking when you decided to sneak a quickie

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.340
in the morning under the same roof as your little sister?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.060
I told you, that's not what this is.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.480
Right, Natsumi?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.970
You're so dirty, Shidou-kun.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.850
Why are you even in your adult form?!

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:35.320
Oh, right. I guess I didn't tell you about her yet.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.580
What happened? Do I need to seal her powers again?

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.880
No, you sealed her powers just fine.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.300
So something pushed Natsumi's mind into the gutter?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.620
Well, I guess you could say that...

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.200
Wasn't her mental state fragile to begin with?

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.980
Hey, don't leave me out of the conversation.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:57.750
You're making me feel like an outsider here.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.380
Listen, you can't just keep transforming whenever you feel like it.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.360
Don't get jealous just because he's pining for me now.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.390
But I guess it is a fact that my body's in a whole different league than yours.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.260
Wha—

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.820
Do you think I'm some midget?!

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.650
I'm just getting into my growth spurt!

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.400
"Midget?"

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.920
Don't laugh at me!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.530
I'm not making fun of you.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.530
Shut up!

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.030
<i>Origami's still not here?</i>

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.900
<i>She was wearing a DEM CR-Unit.</i>

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.040
<i>Why though?</i>

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.020
<i>Why would she...</i>

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.480
Stand.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.620
Bow.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.780
Sit.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:52.430
Before we take attendance,
 I have a bit of a sad announcement to make.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.060
Huh? What's up, Tama-chan?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.310
Did your blind date go badly?
 Were you too eager to get married?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.110
That's so gross!

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.230
Ahem.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:07.480
Actually, due to unforeseen circumstances,
 Tobiichi Origami-san will be transferring...

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:08.240
Transferring?!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.740
Trans... fur?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.750
Wait, Origami's transferring? Why?!

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.420
I don't really know too much about her reasons.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:22.380
She just called all of a sudden and told me she was transferring

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.880
and that she'd send the necessary paperwork over later.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.010
Wh-What school is she transferring to?!

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:32.270
Um, I only heard that she'd be transferring to a school in England.

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:33.820
England...

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.270
Don't tell me...

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.400
Itsuka-kun?

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.200
U-Uh, oh god, my stomach!

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.060
My stomach hurts!

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:45.420
Shid—

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.360
You don't need to come with me, Tohka.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.120
Ow, ow...

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.000
Why am I always like this?!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.870
I was able to wake up early, but then I...

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:01.720
I didn't mean to wake him up like that.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.010
Thanks for the tea, Natsumi-chan.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.890
U-Uh, do you need something from me?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.390
Um, well...

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.500
<i>What did she come here for?</i>

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.040
<i>Why would she come here?</i>

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.280
<i>O-Oh no! Maybe she's here to get her revenge on me!</i>

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:30.900
I-I just thought that since this is your first time here,

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.660
you might not know your way around town yet.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.920
<i>I almost forgot.</i>

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:39.670
<i>I transformed into her best friend,
 that puppet, in order to fool Shidou.</i>

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.500
I-I'm not an expert on the city either, though...

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.050
I don't know how helpful I'll be, but...

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.180
<i>She has to be here to get back at me while Shidou and the others aren't here.</i>

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:53.930
If you'd like, I could show you around town.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:54.930
Huh?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.780
While everyone's at school, I'm normally by myself,

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:05.150
but now that you're here, I thought maybe we could hang out and talk.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.780
W-We're friends, after all!

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:08.760
<i>Whoa...</i>

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.530
<i>What's going on? I want to marry her!</i>

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.980
Y-You're going to take me around town, right? Let's go!

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.100
Let's get going!

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.540
Let's go right now!

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:24.000
The number you have dialed can not be reached at this time—

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.300
Why aren't you picking up?!

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.800
Please be here, Origami!

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.680
I'm glad I was able to get in.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:47.690
T{*\fs40.857}o{*\fs41.714}b{*\fs42.571}i{*\fs43.429}i{*\fs44.286}c{*\fs45.143}hi

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.690
Origami, it's me! 
Answer me if you're there!

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:53.700
T{*\fs39.857}o{*\fs39.714}b{*\fs39.571}i{*\fs39.429}i{*\fs39.286}c{*\fs39.143}hi

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.950
It's open?

00:07:58.440 --> 00:07:59.200
Origami!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:06.000
Where did you go, Origami?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.160
Your lunch looks so good, Kotori-chan!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.100
Onii-chan made it for me!

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.350
Let's eat!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.340
You can't reach Shidou?

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:24.940
Isn't that because he's at school?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.730
He left early after hearing that
 Tobiichi Origami had transferred.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.280
What?

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:34.990
Something doesn't sound right about this.
  Where are Tohka and the others?

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:39.740
Tohka, the Yamai sisters, and Miku are all having lunch at their respective schools.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.750
Natsumi and Yoshino are wandering around the city.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:49.360
I see. I don't want to worry any of them,
 but we can't hide this forever.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:52.960
Find Shidou before they get back from school.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.000
Where am I?

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.150
I was looking for Origami, and then...

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.800
Origami!

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.780
Origami, you—

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.100
Water.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.700
You must be thirsty.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.660
Stop! I'll have some...

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.980
Just let me drink it normally!

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:35.050
Could you lift it slow—

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.560
C-Could you take these off of me now?

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.920
I can't.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.570
Did you really join DEM?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:52.780
Yes.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:56.980
Did you kidnap me on Westcott's orders?

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.600
Bringing you here was my decision.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.700
DEM has no idea any of this is happening.

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:07.320
I had no choice.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:12.090
This is the best way to keep you from getting caught up in what's about to happen.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.480
Wait a second.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.220
What are you stopping me from getting caught up in?

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.940
The battle between me and the Spirits.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.220
The Spirits?!

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:26.060
Of course, Yatogami Tohka and the others are no exception.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.560
Aren't you after the Spirit that killed your parents?!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.690
Tohka and the others have nothing to do with that!

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.660
They're still Spirits.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:41.780
I can't let them roam freely and risk others falling into the same despair that I've felt.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.820
None of them are anywhere near as powerful as they were!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.790
Why would you target them as they are now?!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.740
The Japan Ground Forces may think that way...

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.790
But I'm under no obligation to follow their philosophy any longer.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.300
Tell me, Origami...

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.050
It's been half a year since Tohka transferred into our school.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.970
Time flies. Seriously.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:09.770
The Spirits you hunted for so long are now a part of our daily lives.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.060
All of them are trying to live as humans.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:19.070
Can you really say that nothing's changed for you even after living among them all this time?!

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:23.820
You can't seriously believe that Spirits can't change...
 that they're too dangerous to let live!

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.950
But I do!

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.940
Yatogami Tohka and all the other Spirits will never change.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:34.260
They're part of my revenge.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.210
That's how it was supposed to be...

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.340
But I couldn't forgive myself for how I slowly drifted away from that belief.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:45.840
I swore to kill all Spirits on that day five years ago.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:50.730
It troubled me that I was getting so used to this daily life.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.920
I joined DEM because I came to that realization.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:02.110
I couldn't forgive myself for living a life
 side by side with Spirits like Yatogami Tohka.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.820
Why is it such a bad thing?!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:06.860
You know it's not, don't you?!

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:09.830
Tohka and the others just want to live a normal life!

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.780
And I can't forgive that.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.090
Not as long as they're Spirits.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:19.400
They're not the only ones I have to kill.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:23.590
I have to kill myself—the one who let herself lose sight of her goal.

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:29.100
After killing Yatogami Tohka, I'll regain who I am.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:32.980
Wait, Origami! Please, wait!

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:40.340
Are you sure about letting her act on her own, Ike?

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:41.740
It's fine.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.680
She's all fired up.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:49.240
I don't think there's any need to dampen a young wizard's spirits.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.840
Our goal is the Spirits.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.500
And even if she shot down a bomb,

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.250
we still don't have a good read on her power just yet.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:03.130
Don't you want to see how far she can go?

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.510
Fine. We'll sit back and watch.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.380
You seem displeased.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:12.640
It's easy to tell. You furrow your brow when you lie.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.160
Just a joke.

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:18.600
Don't get so mad.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:22.280
I'd like you to pursue a different target.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.180
A different target?

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:24.780
Yes.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.620
Ratatosk.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:31.900
I want you to slow them down.
 They're sure to get in Tobiichi Origami's way.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.040
Make sure to use Goetia.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:37.240
Why did Shidou leave school early?

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.100
We really need to do some training, though.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:42.740
Agreement: We're total weaklings.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:45.300
Let's start running tomorrow.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.760
I bet Shido had his reasons!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:52.780
Question: I heard that Master Origami
 is transferring out of our school.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:55.810
Do you think Shidou leaving early had something to do with that?

00:13:56.080 --> 00:14:01.070
Yes. After he heard that she transferred, he ran out the door.

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:05.190
I knew it! This smells fishy.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.500
It smells?

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.320
I don't smell anything.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.570
No, that's not what I meant.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.060
Tohka-san!

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.380
Kaguya-san!

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:20.830
Yuzuru-san!

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.840
Why are you dodging my expression of love?

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.340
I-Is that what that was?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:27.860
Yes, it was.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.800
Everyone does it.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.350
Come on, Tohka-san. You too!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.100
Underling, do not be deceived!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.700
Warning: This stinks of lies.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.040
I knew it!

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.480
What are you even doing here, Miku?

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.000
Oh, right.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.800
I came to see Darling, but nobody was home and I became terribly bored.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.110
Nobody was home in the apartments next door either.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.040
Shido's not back yet?

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:54.340
This might really have something to do with Origami.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:57.250
Agreement: Something might have happened to him.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.560
Aw come on, fill me in on what's going on!

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.380
Did something happen to Darling?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.130
Well...

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.220
Is this...

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:07.640
The spacequake alarm.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.480
Did a new Spirit show up?

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:13.440
Curiosity: I'm interested to see what kind of Spirit has appeared.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:18.020
No! The alarm's ringing, so we have to take shelter!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.520
But Shido—

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.020
Don't worry about him.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.520
Tobiichi Origami?!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.270
Why are you here?!

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:27.150
There's no spacequake.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:28.500
What do you mean?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:29.780
Everyone's running for shelter.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:33.410
I made the alarms go off.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.790
But there will be no Spirits or AST showing up.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.790
What? Why would you do that?!

