{=4}T{*\fs22.067}o{*\fs22.133}b{*\fs22.2}i{*\fs22.267}i{*\fs22.333}c{*\fs22.4}h{*\fs22.467}i {*\fs22.6}O{*\fs22.667}r{*\fs22.733}i{*\fs22.8}g{*\fs22.867}a{*\fs22.933}mi

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:01.060
What are you doing?!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:05.690
Didn't you hear me? I'm going to kill all of you Spirits!

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.320
Her eyes... Why?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.860
Why did you change back to your old self, Tobiichi Origami?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:17.870
Good instincts.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.750
Admiration: I'm impressed, Master Origami.

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:24.500
We'll hear out your excuse for this.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.540
Interrogating: Please tell us, Master Origami.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.760
I don't wish to fight you.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.720
I have no reason to tell you anything!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.520
Sandalphon!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.620
Gabriel, rondo!

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:59.660
Are you all okay?!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:03.420
Tobiichi Origami is serious.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.420
It's kill or be killed.

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:08.780
But...

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:10.420
Wake up, Tohka!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.180
Tobiichi Origami? What's she doing here?

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.500
These magic levels are off the chart!

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.810
These aren't like anything we've seen before!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.810
They don't stand a chance against her in their limited astral dresses.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:26.310
Fraxinus, full speed ahead.
 We're going to get them out of there.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.040
Deploy Yggdrafolium just in case.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:30.580
We're going to help them!

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:32.070
Roger.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.070
What happened?!

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.480
We've been hit. Territory has fallen to thirty percent functionality!

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.320
Enemy at three o'clock!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.950
This reading... It's an enemy ship!

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.450
What?!

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:48.580
That's a DEM ship!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:49.460
Now of all times?!

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.460
Incoming transmission!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:51.400
Transmission?

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:55.160
The Fraxinus is receiving a transmission from the enemy ship.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:56.240
Patch it in!

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:56.590
Roger.

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.620
I suppose I should start by saying, "Nice to meet you."

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.720
Thank you for accepting my transmission.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.350
Ellen Mathers?!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.340
You know of me?

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:10.230
What an honor, Itsuka Kotori.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:14.860
So what does the strongest wizard in the world want with us?

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.440
If you want to have a tea party, do you mind waiting?

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:18.900
We're a little busy right now.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:23.120
Looks like some kid from an evil company's picking a fight with some of our own.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.900
I have two points of business.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:31.880
First, anyone who values their lives should evacuate within the next three minutes.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:37.130
Are you saying you're going to shoot down our ship?

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:41.060
I can't deny that after all's said and done,
 that won't be the end result.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:43.350
But, that name... "Fraxinus."

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.400
It means "World Tree," doesn't it?

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:47.270
I assume that's Elliot's doing?

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:52.270
I get the feeling you're not taking us seriously.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:57.340
I believe you're the one who's
 underestimating their opponent.

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:00.530
You underestimate both my and Goetia's power

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.530
So what was your other point of business?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.720
For those who flee from this battle,

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:09.280
I'd like them to convey a message to Elliot.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:10.260
A message?

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.360
Yes.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:15.080
Elliot, Elliot, you damn traitor!

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.680
You traitor who turned your back on the vow we made!

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.060
Be ready for what's coming!

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:23.300
Wherever you're hiding, I'll find you,
 and personally remove your head from your shoulders!

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:26.960
That's all.

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:30.240
I'll wait three minutes starting now.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.940
I encourage you all to run.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:34.180
You hear that?

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:37.940
Our opponent is the strongest person on Earth. 
I grant permission to anyone who'd like to run.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.440
No way.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:44.400
If this was enough to make me want to run,
 I would've run away a long time ago.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:48.700
Deserting you, commander?
 That's basically like dying anyway.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:54.220
Agreed! I don't care if she's the strongest in the world,
 we'll show her what we're made of.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:56.000
Please give us your orders, Commander.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.590
Victory's as good as ours.

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:03.090
I have my PC rigged so that when I die,
 my D-drive will be wiped!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.200
Of course.

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:07.850
But it might be nice to feel the
 Commander's wrath if I ran away—

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:10.980
You get all that?

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.980
I see. How disappointing.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:16.730
AR-008! Divert parallel driving force to numbers three through six.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.200
Begin charging magic.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:19.540
Prepare Mystletainn!

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:21.940
Target the DEM ship, Goetia!

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:22.740
Roger!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:28.140
I thought you were capable of more rational decisions than this, Itsuka Kotori.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:32.280
Even if you're not blood related,
 you truly are Itsuka Shidou's little sister.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:33.750
You flatter me.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:37.660
Kannazuki, deploy Yggdrafolium one through twelve.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.500
We're fighting with the strongest wizard.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.130
Get it ready just in case.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.380
I knew you'd ask.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:48.140
Let's wrap this up then go save Tohka and the others!

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.120
Charging complete, Mystletainn is ready to fire!

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:53.020
No movement from the enemy ship.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:57.150
She really is waiting the full three minutes.
 How condescending...

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:58.400
Mystletainn, fire!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.570
What the... What was that movement?!

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:11.080
It looks like she's reduced the ship's territory to the bare minimum to increase its mobility.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:16.080
Most likely she used the territory to fling herself in that direction.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.210
Is that even possible?!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:20.940
It's possible in theory and in practice.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:23.980
I suppose this is why she's lauded as the strongest wizard—

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:25.470
This isn't the time to be impressed!

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.340
Incoming!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.220
Change territory to defense!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.720
Brace for impact!

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:35.580
Not bad.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:36.820
Counterattack!

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:40.360
Change Yggdrafolium to cloak us and get behind her!

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.110
Roger!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:44.860
What's going on?

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:46.860
She's shooting again!

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:02.460
Damn it! Someone! Is anyone there?!

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:04.970
Somebody!

